WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.840
Utah seeks up to $61.2 million from kalshi and its market makers. This is Prediction Markets Daily, episode 29. Journalism and education never abet. After that filing Robinhood's October contract count, crypto exchanges applying for US licenses, a CFTC forum agenda, then the board and a study of what a displayed price does to a voter. Derek Brown, Utah's attorney general, filed that case on October 20 in Utah State Court.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:35.060
He named five Kalshi entities and two Susquehanna firms, and he wants preliminary and permanent

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:41.680
injunctions covering sports, election, politics, culture, and mentions contracts, plus restitution

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:45.240
and access limits run through a court-approved geolocation provider.

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:48.720
Filing the complaint does not itself impose those limits.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.820
Utah has not regulated any form of gambling.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:56.900
Intergame reported Brown's view that the contracts are indistinguishable from sportsbook

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:03.060
bets, and via Fox 13, that residents have lost between $36 million and $66 million

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:08.020
through CalShe since February, with almost 33,000 accounts in the state.

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:19.460
Token Post reported a separate fee estimate, $30,591,600 to $61,183,200 as of October 19,

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:22.160
and called that range an extrapolation.

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:30.000
Calche's own count was 32,940 fully signed up accounts with Utah addresses as of February 25,

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:35.680
which does not show who was physically in the state. Cryptopolitan reported the claim that

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:41.460
Susquehanna International Group and Susquehanna Government Products act as market makers taking the

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:46.880
other side of retail trades. Those claims are not yet verified and neither company has been shown

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:52.940
liable. Jackie McGavick, a Cal She spokesperson, told CoinTelegraph that Cal She is a federally

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:57.660
regulated financial exchange, that customers trade with each other and set the prices,

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:02.220
that it answers to the CFTC, that no single state should have a veto,

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:06.500
and that this state court action does not affect its ongoing federal litigation.

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:12.560
An August 4th federal ruling found commodities law did not bar Utah from applying its gambling

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:18.760
laws to Kalshi's sports contracts. Kalshi appealed, and on September 8th, an appeals court rejected

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:24.996
its bid for interim relief. Vlad Tenev, speaking this week at Yahoo Finance's Invest Conference,

00:02:25.496 --> 00:02:31.116
said Robinhood's prediction markets unit traded roughly 2.5 billion event contracts in October,

00:02:31.696 --> 00:02:35.936
more than all of the third quarter combined. He called it the biggest product launch in the

00:02:35.936 --> 00:02:41.776
company's history. Start-up fortune carried the remarks. At a penny-a-contract, Yahoo Finance

00:02:41.776 --> 00:02:47.816
put October fees at about $25 million, which that piece says implies roughly $300 million

00:02:47.816 --> 00:02:54.136
in annualized revenue. Double the prior quarter's run rate. Robinhood launched event contracts in

00:02:54.136 --> 00:03:01.536
March 2026. It already works with Calche, ForecastEX, and Rothera, a CFTC licensed exchange

00:03:01.536 --> 00:03:07.676
built with Susquehanna. Rothera has processed more than 3.5 billion contracts since late May,

00:03:07.676 --> 00:03:13.936
about 93% of them, FIFA World Cup markets. From September 8th, Robin Hood began

00:03:13.936 --> 00:03:19.436
routing a selection of college and pro football contracts to OG.com. A CFTC

00:03:19.436 --> 00:03:25.716
regulated exchange, crypto.com operates. CalShi posted a record 19.03 billion

00:03:25.716 --> 00:03:30.416
dollars in weekly contract volume for October 5th to 11th. That piece notes

00:03:30.416 --> 00:03:35.476
CalShi counts $1 face value contracts, while polymarket tracks takeer side

00:03:35.476 --> 00:03:41.698
cash volume. Blockchain.com last week applied for a U.S. license to offer regulated prediction

00:03:41.698 --> 00:03:48.458
markets, and Binance U.S. has sought regulatory approval, joining Coinbase, crypto.com and Gemini.

00:03:49.138 --> 00:03:53.978
Hedgeweek reported that from a financial times account. The block figures in the same report

00:03:53.978 --> 00:03:59.618
show trading volume on polymarket and CalSHE up more than 300 percent from $17 billion

00:03:59.618 --> 00:04:06.318
dollars in January to $72 billion in September, while spot crypto trading volumes fell 18 percent.

00:04:06.738 --> 00:04:11.358
Michigan regulators said this month that Coinbase had agreed to stop offering event contracts

00:04:11.358 --> 00:04:15.658
to customers in the state. Coinbase partnered with Kalshi earlier this year.

00:04:16.258 --> 00:04:20.758
Crypto.com spun out OG.com last month and sold stakes to Robinhood.

00:04:21.338 --> 00:04:24.618
Bullish has applied for a US license to offer event contracts.

00:04:24.618 --> 00:04:31.810
The CFTC's innovation task force released the agenda for its inaugural frontier forum on superintelligence.

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:34.730
That is an announcement of a meeting, not a rule.

00:04:35.390 --> 00:04:40.370
Chairman Michael S. Selig said superintelligence is poised to transform US financial markets,

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:45.450
and that the forum is meant to explore opportunities and risks while protecting market participants.

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:48.830
The meeting will be streamed on cftc.gov.

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:54.777
Metacaculous said it has produced two forecast maps on how much of an AIPO windfall would

00:04:54.777 --> 00:04:56.517
reach charities by cause area.

00:04:57.137 --> 00:05:02.697
A CalShi question on which party wins the U.S. House sits on the board today at a 90.7 percent

00:05:02.697 --> 00:05:04.997
implied probability for the Democratic Party.

00:05:05.797 --> 00:05:12.097
Polymarkets Brazil presidential market prices Flavio Bolsonaro at 80 percent, up 3.2 points

00:05:12.097 --> 00:05:12.657
in a day.

00:05:12.657 --> 00:05:19.217
Gadi Eisenkott is at 51.5% on polymarkets market for Prime Minister of Israel after the

00:05:19.217 --> 00:05:19.897
next election.

00:05:20.617 --> 00:05:27.037
Kalshi's 2028 Democratic presidential nominee market prices Gavin Newsom at 17%, John

00:05:27.037 --> 00:05:32.297
Ossoff at 16%, and Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez at 14%.

00:05:32.297 --> 00:05:38.557
Manifold, which uses play money called mana, not dollars, prices a yes at 32% on whether

00:05:38.557 --> 00:05:44.577
another millennium prize problem is solved in 2026. Access to these venues and to which

00:05:44.577 --> 00:05:49.837
contracts depends on where you live, and availability is not the same in every country, province

00:05:49.837 --> 00:05:50.497
or state.

00:05:51.452 --> 00:05:56.552
Polymarket listed a market asking whether Laurent Nunez is out as France's interior minister.

00:05:57.152 --> 00:06:03.212
The listing, posted October 21, says he has held the post since October 2025, publicly

00:06:03.212 --> 00:06:08.372
offered his resignation, and that President Emanuel Macron rejected it on October 19.

00:06:09.552 --> 00:06:14.472
Wishful prices are hard to separate from information, and how it works here starts with a reader,

00:06:14.732 --> 00:06:20.052
not a trader. A Brennan Center analysis measured what a displayed Calche figure does to someone

00:06:20.052 --> 00:06:26.372
who never put money down. It does not track traders' own politics. Yeji Lee's write-up, funded by

00:06:26.372 --> 00:06:33.352
the Brennan Center for Justice and released October 20, used a survey of 1,994 self-identified

00:06:33.352 --> 00:06:39.392
registered voters fielded September 21. Each person saw five pairs of hypothetical congressional

00:06:39.392 --> 00:06:46.612
candidates. Profiles listed race, age, party, and previous occupation. Plus an NBC news poll estimate

00:06:46.612 --> 00:06:52.192
and a Calche chance that researchers vary at random. Random assignment is how the design tries to

00:06:52.192 --> 00:06:57.192
pull the price away from the biography and the poll. If the Calche figure still changes the pick,

00:06:57.692 --> 00:07:02.952
the number is doing work of its own. A candidate shown at 50% on Calche is the baseline.

00:07:03.352 --> 00:07:10.312
Move that displayed figure to 67% and respondents were 10 percentage points more likely to name that candidate the winner.

00:07:10.752 --> 00:07:13.892
Move it to 84% and the gain was 20 points.

00:07:14.412 --> 00:07:18.572
At 33%, respondents were 11 points less likely to pick the candidate.

00:07:19.052 --> 00:07:22.072
At 16%, they were 19 points less likely.

00:07:22.712 --> 00:07:27.272
Lee's write-up says the market figure moved perceptions about as much as the traditional poll did,

00:07:27.692 --> 00:07:30.092
and more than any background trait in the profile.

00:07:30.092 --> 00:07:36.032
A warning that asked people to be careful about prediction markets had no effect on how much they used the figure.

00:07:36.672 --> 00:07:43.892
Only 19% of respondents said election prediction markets are accurate against 37% who said that of traditional polls.

00:07:44.492 --> 00:07:49.892
Just 29% said the markets reflect public opinion against 55% for polls.

00:07:50.292 --> 00:07:58.232
37% neither agreed nor disagreed that the markets are accurate, and 29% took no position on whether they represent the public.

00:07:58.232 --> 00:08:01.772
People who do not trust the number still moved when it was shown.

00:08:02.352 --> 00:08:05.792
48% said prediction markets should be regulated more strongly.

00:08:06.332 --> 00:08:08.712
23% said some types should be banned.

00:08:09.232 --> 00:08:14.772
16% said all of them should be banned, and 14% said they should not be regulated at all.

00:08:15.312 --> 00:08:19.892
The analysis cited polling that seven in 10 Americans disapprove of betting on elections,

00:08:19.892 --> 00:08:26.012
and a Reuters Ipsos poll released October 12th that found 60% of US adults oppose using

00:08:26.012 --> 00:08:28.452
prediction markets to wager on election results.

00:08:28.912 --> 00:08:31.492
The Brennan Center's reason for caring is structural.

00:08:31.972 --> 00:08:38.012
It said more than $220 million has been wagered on the 2026 midterms, and that election

00:08:38.012 --> 00:08:44.272
figures now reach the public through partnerships with outlets including CNN, CNBC, and Fox News.

00:08:44.712 --> 00:08:48.152
This show takes no money from any venue and holds no position.

00:08:48.152 --> 00:08:55.092
RG.org noted that a CNN analysis put trading on 2026 election contracts at CalShe and

00:08:55.092 --> 00:08:57.872
Polymarket above $750 million.

00:08:58.842 --> 00:09:04.272
After Minnesota enacted a law this year banning CalShe and Polymarket, the companies persuaded

00:09:04.272 --> 00:09:06.812
a federal judge to block it before it took effect.

00:09:07.492 --> 00:09:13.592
The CFTC this month proposed classifying event contracts as swaps, with a companion interim

00:09:13.592 --> 00:09:19.052
rule keeping sportsbook wagers and casino games outside that definition. Nothing in the

00:09:19.052 --> 00:09:24.312
design observes an order, a position, or a partisan account. A display other people can

00:09:24.312 --> 00:09:29.932
trade against was never tested. The experiment tests the reader. Set a market number beside

00:09:29.932 --> 00:09:35.112
a poll and a method. The Brennan Center's own line is that asking voters to discount the

00:09:35.112 --> 00:09:41.302
figure is easier said than done. Before we go, blockchain.com's U.S. license application

00:09:41.302 --> 00:09:45.142
for prediction markets is in, and an application is not an approval.

00:09:45.782 --> 00:09:50.402
That's prediction markets daily for today. Nothing in this show is financial advice,

00:09:50.862 --> 00:09:55.102
and if trading or betting has stopped being fun, help is available where you live.

